{title: Living for Jesus}
{artist: Thomas Chisholm & C. Harold Lowden}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[F]Living for Jesus a [Bb]life that is [F]true, [Gm]striving to [C]please him in [F]all that I do,
yielding allegiance, glad-[Bb]hearted and [F]free — [Gm]this is the [C]pathway of [F]blessing for me.

Chorus
O [Bb]Jesus, Lord and [F]Savior, I [C]give myself to [F]thee,
for [Bb]thou in thy a[F]tonement didst [G]give thyself for [C]me;
I [F]own no other [Bb]master — my [F]heart shall be thy [Dm]throne:
my [F]life I give, hence[C]forth to live, O [F]Christ, for [C]thee a[F]lone.
